# Product C++: C++23 + traits

## Language standard

Product C++ under **`src/`**, **`core/`**, **`testing/`**, and **`algorithm/`** is **C++23**. Windows `cc_std = "c++23"` maps to MSVC `/std:c++23preview` (v145 ignores `/std:c++23` until 14.52). That is the floor. Do not use `/std:c++latest`. Do not drop back to C++17. Linux/mac keep `-std=c++23`.

New code and touched translation units use this standard. **`third_party/`** is out of scope — do not force third-party CMake (GDAL, etc.) onto `cc_std`. Do not rewrite **`branches/`** (if present). Legacy `src/` MFC / 2010 TUs must **compile** as C++23 once the flag is on; do not drive-by rewrite them to concepts.

## Do (portable C++20 / C++23)

- Use `concepts`, `requires`, `if constexpr`, `std::invoke_result_t`, `std::is_same_v`, ranges where MSVC v145 is fine, NTTP where MSVC v145 accepts them.
- Prefer **traits + concepts** over parallel class trees, copied 2D vs 3D functions, and macros.

## Don't (language)

- Don't target C++17, or pin `/std:c++17` on product targets.
- Don't require fold-expressions-in-`requires`, GCC `__integer_pack`, or other non-MSVC constructs.
- Don't treat `/std:c++23` as the Windows default **cl flag** on 14.50/14.51 (use `/std:c++23preview`; `cc_std` stays `"c++23"`).

## Traits / TMP

One **Geometry** hierarchy; OGC `coordinateDimension` is **2 or 3** on the **instance** (not `Geometry2` / `Geometry3`). Compile-time `dimension` / `has_z` belong on math vectors (`Vector2` vs `Vector3`) and on backend traits. Algorithms key off `geometry_traits<G>` (`coordinate_type`, accessors) plus `g.coordinate_dimension()`, not a 2D vs 3D type name. Dispatch **GEOS / PROJ / TIN** backends through traits so product types stay stable.

Keep existing **`Smt_*` virtual ABI** where LoadLibrary / DLL exports require it. New algorithms must not add another virtual geometry hierarchy.

Public namespaces stay two levels (`geo`, helpers in `geo::detail`). Traits types are public API at those two levels. New-tree functions stay `snake_case`.

YAGNI: traits exist to collapse 2D/3D and backend dispatch — not to invent an in-tree Boost.Geometry.

```cpp
namespace geo {

template <typename G>
struct geometry_traits {
  using coordinate_type = typename G::coordinate_type;
  static int coordinate_dimension(const G& g);  // 2 or 3, instance
};

template <typename V>
struct vector_traits {
  using coordinate_type = typename V::coordinate_type;
  static constexpr int dimension = V::dimension;  // 2, 3, or 4
};

template <typename G>
concept geometry_like = requires(const G& g) {
  typename geometry_traits<G>::coordinate_type;
  geometry_traits<G>::coordinate_dimension(g);
};

template <typename G>
struct geos_backend_traits;  // specialize per product type; call geos_c

template <geometry_like G>
void buffer(const G& g, typename geometry_traits<G>::coordinate_type width) {
  geos_backend_traits<G>::buffer(g, width);
}

}  // namespace geo
```

## Prefer traits + concepts (from mogu `cpp20-traits`)

Prefer **traits + concepts** over duplicated if/else families and parallel helper copies:

- `concept` / `requires` for capabilities
- trait types (`is_*`, `*_traits`) and `if constexpr` for compile-time dispatch
- customization via **trait specialization**, not God-classes

This repo **targets MSVC v145** as well as GCC/Clang. Portable C++20/23 is required; do **not** copy mogu’s “no `#ifdef _MSC_VER` / MSVC may fail” stance. Windows `cc_std` stays `"c++23"` → `/std:c++23preview`.

## Don't (product)

- Don't add Qt.
- Don't vendor a second GEOS / PROJ (use the shipped `gdal_sdk` stack).
- Don't put a parallel 2D/3D type tree next to Geometry.
- **Don't** TMP for its own sake on trivial one-liners.
- **Don't** invent an in-tree Boost.Geometry or a second virtual geometry hierarchy.
